# Response headers for the static assets and the HTML document.
#
# This file only covers what Pages serves from dist/. Function responses set
# their own headers in server/http.ts (no-store, nosniff, Referrer-Policy), so
# the API is not affected by anything here.
#
# Every external origin below is one the app actually loads from. Adding an
# origin is a decision to trust it with script execution or data; removing one
# breaks whatever used it. The current set:
#   accounts.google.com      Google Identity Services (script + its iframe,
#                            plus the GSI stylesheet it injects)
#   www.googletagmanager.com Google Analytics loader
#   *.google-analytics.com   Analytics beacons
#   static.cloudflareinsights.com Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon (Pages
#                            injects this automatically when analytics is on)
#   cloudflareinsights.com   Where that beacon posts its RUM data
#   fonts.googleapis.com     Font stylesheet, @import'ed from src/index.css
#   fonts.gstatic.com        The font files themselves
#
# frame-src carries 'self' so src/pages/DocumentDetails.tsx can frame a stored PDF
# from /api/storage. Note object-src stays 'none': <object>/<embed> are a plugin
# surface we have no use for, and an <iframe> covers the same need.
#   lh3.googleusercontent.com Google profile pictures
#
# Two notes for whoever edits this next:
#
# 1. style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' because React writes inline style
#    attributes (progress bars, confidence meters). script-src deliberately does
#    NOT get it. The JSON-LD block in index.html is an inline <script>, so a
#    strict script-src makes the browser log a refusal for it. Nothing breaks:
#    application/ld+json is never executed, and crawlers parse the HTML without
#    applying CSP. Do not add 'unsafe-inline' to script-src to silence it.
#
# 2. connect-src lists ONLY origins the browser still talks to directly. It used
#    to also carry https://api.futureppo.top, https://api.openai.com and
#    https://*.amazonaws.com, for a "browser-side fallback" that reached the OCR
#    vendors from the page. That path no longer exists -- src/lib/ocr-client.ts
#    states outright that there is no direct-to-provider fallback, because a
#    browser cannot hold the credential. Leaving the origins here kept open the
#    exact channel the key-leak fix closed: with an XSS, a page could have posted
#    every extracted document straight out to them. Do not re-add a vendor origin
#    unless the browser genuinely calls it.
#
# 3. api.emailjs.com is deliberately absent. The /contact form used to reach it
#    directly, which required a service id, template id and public key in the
#    bundle -- the full argument set for its send endpoint. That path is gone
#    (see the header of src/pages/legal/Contact.tsx); the credential is a Pages
#    secret and only the Worker uses it, where CSP does not apply. Do not re-add
#    this origin: doing so is what a browser-side send would need.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://lh3.googleusercontent.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: unsafe-none
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Hashed build output is immutable, so it can be cached hard. The HTML document
# is not hashed and must not be, or a deploy would not reach anyone.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
